<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!-- Hardened runtime for the app and its two helpers (pool-core, pool-runner), which the bundler signs with the same
     identity and this one file. Not App Sandboxed: the app starts the agent, and the agent confines each job runner
     with its own deny-by-default sandbox profile (no network, no user files). No JIT, no DYLD_* environment, no
     debugger attachment.

     One exception: library validation is off. The runner loads the pinned ONNX Runtime pack
     (Resources/backends/ort-cpu/libonnxruntime.dylib), which keeps Microsoft's signature because re-signing it would
     change its pinned bytes. With library validation on, macOS refuses it in our ad-hoc build ("mapping process and
     mapped file (non-platform) have different Team IDs"), and also refuses a copy re-signed ad hoc by us, so no
     embedding job or benchmark can run on a Mac (measured on macOS 27, T-225). What still decides which library
     loads: the agent and the runner both check the pack's SHA-256 pins right before it is loaded, by full path, and
     the job runs in the sandbox. The bundler cannot give one helper its own entitlements, so the exception applies
     to all three; to be narrowed to pool-runner, or dropped, once a Developer ID signs the pack (CR-T215-01). -->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
